<ChapterLayout
  title="3.3 — Formation and Evolution of Stars · AST 100"
  description="How stars are born inside cold hydrogen clouds, and how their mass decides everything that follows — a small star's quiet end as a white dwarf, or a massive star's supernova that forges the elements of planets and people."
